  "summary": "Independent writer Larry Kubin toured San Francisco documenting the city's growing surveillance infrastructure, including SFPD's ~400 Flock ALPRs, drones, and the Real Time Investigation Center. The article situates his findings amid recent disclosures that NCRIC and out-of-state agencies improperly accessed SFPD Flock data, prompting SFPD to stop sharing with NCRIC and WSIN, and amid Proposition E's loosening of policy oversight.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Police Chief Derrick Lew said last week that out-of-state and federal law enforcement agencies had \u201cimproperly\u201d accessed the data, after the Northern California Regional Intelligence Center queried the system hundreds of times.",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    },
    {
      "quote": "The incident prompted SFPD to stop sharing Flock data with NCRIC and another agency, the Western States Information Network.",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    },
    {
      "quote": "Bay Area cities Santa Cruz, Mountain View, El Cerrito and the town of Los Altos Hills have canceled Flock contracts over similar concerns surrounding improper data sharing",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    },
    {
      "quote": "The 2024 ballot measure gave SFPD the green light to roll out new surveillance technology for a full year without an official policy.",
      "paragraph_idx": 18
    }
  ],
